# .trivyignore — deferred CVEs with tracking notes.
# Each entry here has an explicit reason and a tracking ticket/PR.
# Review quarterly; remove entries when the root upgrade lands.

# ── @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node + @opentelemetry/sdk-node ───────
# CVE: CVE-2026-44902 (HIGH) — Prometheus exporter crash via malformed HTTP request
# Fix: upgrade @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node 0.51.0→0.75.0,
#       @opentelemetry/sdk-node 0.53.0→0.217.0
# Reason: 0.51→0.75 is a 24-minor-version jump in the OTel ecosystem; requires
#         thorough compatibility testing with the rest of the instrumentation stack.
# Track:  open a "chore: update otel deps" PR against main.
CVE-2026-44902

# ── fast-uri (transitive via fastify) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE: CVE-2026-6321 (HIGH) — Path traversal via URI parsing
# CVE: CVE-2026-6322 (HIGH) — percent-encoded authority delimiter bypass
# Fix: fast-uri 3.1.2+ — but fast-uri 3.x is only pulled in by fastify 5.x.
# Reason: fast-uri is a transitive dep of fastify 4.x; the fix requires
#         upgrading fastify to 5.x which is a breaking major-version change.
#         Deferred to the fastify-5 upgrade PR.
# Track:  see CVE-2026-25223 below.
CVE-2026-6321
CVE-2026-6322

# ── fastify ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE: CVE-2026-25223 (HIGH) — Validation bypass via malformed Content-Type header
# Fix: fastify 5.7.2+ (MAJOR version, currently on 4.29.1)
# Reason: fastify 4→5 is a breaking major version change. The migration requires
#         adapting plugin APIs, lifecycle hooks, and the type system. Not safe
#         to take on the soc2-security-floor branch. Requires a dedicated PR
#         with full smoke-test + integration-test pass.
# Track:  open "chore: upgrade fastify 4→5" PR against main.
CVE-2026-25223

